# DVC honours this file, NOT .gitignore. Anything reachable under a stage's
# directory dependency is hashed, so a file git ignores still makes the stage
# stale -- and it does so only on the machine that lacks it. On 2026-09-13 a
# tag looked fully reproducible here and showed six stale stages on another
# clone, because these paths were being hashed into the submodule deps.

# Julia dev-environment manifests, resolved per machine. The manifest that
# picks the versions actually under test is experiments/AMIP/Manifest-v1.11.toml
# and is declared explicitly by the AMIP stages, so it is untouched here. The
# root Manifest.toml is a real dependency too -- these patterns start at */ so
# they cannot match it.
*/Manifest.toml
*/test/Manifest.toml
*/.dev/format/Manifest.toml

# Tooling state that lands inside a submodule checkout. The superproject's own
# .calkit/ is NOT matched: these patterns require a leading directory, and
# .calkit/notebooks/cleaned/ is a declared input to compare-kernels.
*/.calkit/
/ClimaCoupler.jl/experiments/ClimaEarth/

# Editor, OS and language scratch that varies by machine.
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.cov
